WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.401
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:03.803
This is "Late Night." We hope
you're doing well tonight.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.671
Now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:07.640
During a speech at
the White House yesterday,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.477
President Biden joked
about turning 60 instead of 81.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:16.149
Man, nothing drives home
how very old you are

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:19.085
More than joking you're only 60.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:23.022
That's still
discount bus fare old.

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:25.257
During the White House
turkey pardon yesterday,

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:26.959
President Biden
appeared to mix up

00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:28.761
Taylor Swift and Britney Spears

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:31.197
and, just like that,
lost 30 million votes.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.365
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:35.167
That's right. During the turkey
pardon yesterday,

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.503
President Biden
appeared to mix up

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:37.737
Taylor Swift and Britney Spears.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.005
Wow, that's almost
as bad as the time

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:42.609
former President Trump
called Tim Cook Tim Apple,

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.743
thought Frederick Douglass
was alive,

00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:47.613
called Second Corinthians
"Two Corinthians,"

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:50.984
called Kevin McCarthy Steve,
called Paul Ryan Ron,

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.852
walked out of
an executive order ceremony

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.587
after forgetting to sign
an executive order,

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.923
and suggested injecting
bleach to kill COVID.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.691
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.093
Almost as bad.

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:03.696
Still, Britney and Taylor?

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.097
In a newly released letter,

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:06.866
former President Trump's
physician said

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.735
his overall health is excellent

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.004
and his physical exams
are within normal range.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.272
But take that
with a grain of salt,

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.673
because the letter also said
his coat is shiny

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:16.209
and he's negative
for heartworms.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.944
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:27.820
Also, he wrote -- They scratched
out "Rex" and then his name...

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.555
The White House celebrated
President Biden's birthday

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.190
last night
with an Instagram post

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.192
showing him blowing out
a dozen -- dozens --

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.161
dozens of candles --

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.729
dozens of candles on a cake.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.565
And just a quick question
for the Democratic Party,

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:41.000
is anybody in charge of PR?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.036
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.704
You want people to forget
how old he is,

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.372
and you serve him up
a birthday cake

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:50.877
that looks like a garbage can
fire at a hobo camp?

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.311
Hey, you ever heard of these?

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:55.080
Yeah, those.
That's what you want.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.282
Still says he's 81, but at least
it doesn't set off

00:01:57.282 --> 00:02:00.753
the White House
sprinkler system.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.955
Vice President Kamala Harris
this week launched an account

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:04.790
on the social media
platform Threads

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.926 line:0%
and, just in case,
one on LinkedIn.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.261 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:10.363 line:0%
Just in case.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.567
A lamppost fell on three guests

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.536
yesterday at Disneyland's
Main Street, USA,

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:20.640
and it was still more fun
than The Hall of Presidents.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.775
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:27.246
Authorities in Iowa arrested
a man last week

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.249
after he was allegedly
masturbating

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.451
outside a Kum &amp; Go
convenience store.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.120
[ Laughter ]
This news first reported

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.689
by every one
of my writers today.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.225
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.527
"Hey, boss, did you see
the good news?"

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.061
"Yeah.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.663
It's not good news."

00:02:44.663 --> 00:02:45.498
"Hey, did you hear?"

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.033
"Yeah!

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:51.103
Are you in a line out there?
Get out of here!"

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:52.838
And finally, according
to a new survey,

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:54.240
nearly half of Americans

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.076
are traveling during the holiday
season to visit loved ones.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.911
The other half
are visiting family.

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:01.948
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.316 --> 00:03:06.586
And the writer who wrote
that joke's name is Bryan,

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.688
and if you're...

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.590
if you're his family,
now you know.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.791
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.125
And that was a monologue,
everybody!

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:15.194
We're off and running.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:18.264
It's going to be a good one
tonight.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.366
We got a great show
for you tonight.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:23.235
She is the Emmy-winning
co-host of "CBS Mornings"

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:25.504
and the editor-at-large
of Oprah Daily.

00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:27.306
The winter issue
with Oprah's Favorite Things

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:28.474
is on newsstands now.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.844
Our friend Gayle King
will be on the show.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:34.247
Very happy to have Gayle.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:36.082
He is an Emmy-winning actor,

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.751
and his portrayal
of Logan Roy on "Succession"

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.453
is an all-time
great performance.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:43.455
His acting tutorials are
available now on BBC Maestro.

00:03:43.455 --> 00:03:46.358
Brian Cox will also be here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:50.129
I'm very excited because,
you know,

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:53.332
the finale of "Succession" aired
during the writers strike.

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:55.134
We didn't have the show
during the actors strike.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.136
He hasn't really had a chance
to talk about "Succession."

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.337
I'm very excited
to talk about it.

00:03:58.337 --> 00:03:59.939
Logan Roy is truly
one of the best.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:00.974
And, I mean, I'm probably
just saying that

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:02.942
because he reminds me of my dad.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.944
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.482
His acting --
Oh, sorry. We moved on.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.916
[ Mutters ]

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:13.652
You know her from
"Only Murders in the Building"

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:14.954
and "The Idol."

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.955
She stars in the wonderful film
"The Holdovers,"

00:04:16.955 --> 00:04:18.424
which is in theaters now.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.825
Da'Vine Joy Randolph

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:22.294
will also be joining us,
and that movie is good.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:24.764
That movie is good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.467
Thanksgiving show
Thursday of this week,

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:30.135
the guests are going
to be my parents,

00:04:30.135 --> 00:04:32.170
the guests -- the other guest
is going to be my brother.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:35.507
Also, if you can't wait,
my brother and I have a podcast

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:37.410
called "Family Trips
with the Meyers Brothers."

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.279
And this week,
a very special episode.

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:41.547
We asked our listeners
to call in

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.516
with their Thanksgiving stories.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.517
Very funny.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.918
And then
if you just want to listen,

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.386 line:0%
you can hear people
like Amy Poehler

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:50.189 line:0%
talk about her family trips
or my good friend John Mulaney.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.325 line:0%
Very funny as well.
So that's the podcast.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:55.962
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.963
Moving on,
here at "Late Night,"

00:04:57.963 --> 00:04:59.465
every night
I deliver a monologue

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.867
made up of jokes written
by a diverse team of writers.

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:04.503
As a result, a lot of jokes
come across my desk that,

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:06.739
due to my being
a straight white male,

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.274
